content/.football-data-key

# retired-source stubs: never publish (local build artifacts only)
public/entertainment/_recovered/
public/sports/_recovered/

# transient root redirect stubs: build-routing.py writes ~74 of these per build
# ("legacy forwards: N root stubs -> /entertainment/...") and its own pre-clean
# deletes them at the start of the next run. They are regenerated identically
# every time, so they are build artifacts, not source. They are NOT committed.
# Deliberately not globbed (e.g. /*/index.html) - a genuinely new article dir
# at the root must still show up in `git status`, because build-public-dir.py
# auto-stages new page dirs and a silent gitignore rule would let an author
# forget to `git add` a new page.
